### Layer 5: Frontend -- HighlightText Component

**New file: `/Users/evisdrenova/code/entire/devenv/entire.io/frontend/src/components/HighlightText.tsx`**

This is a pure utility component. Design:

```typescript
interface HighlightTextProps {
  text: string;
  query: string;
  className?: string;          // applied to the root <span>
  highlightClassName?: string; // applied to each <mark>, defaults to yellow highlight
}

export function HighlightText({ text, query, className, highlightClassName }: HighlightTextProps) {
  // If no query or empty query, return plain text
  if (!query.trim()) {
    return <span className={className}>{text}</span>;
  }

  // Split query into individual words, filter empties, escape regex special chars
  const words = query.trim().split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean);
  if (words.length === 0) {
    return <span className={className}>{text}</span>;
  }

  // Build regex: match any word, case-insensitive
  const escaped = words.map(w => w.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, '\\$&'));
  const pattern = new RegExp(`(${escaped.join('|')})`, 'gi');

  // Split text by pattern, preserving matches
  const parts = text.split(pattern);

  const defaultHighlight = "bg-yellow-200/60 dark:bg-yellow-800/40 rounded-sm px-0.5";

  return (
    <span className={className}>
      {parts.map((part, i) => {
        const isMatch = pattern.test(part);
        pattern.lastIndex = 0; // reset regex state
        if (isMatch) {
          return <mark key={i} className={highlightClassName ?? defaultHighlight}>{part}</mark>;
        }
        return <span key={i}>{part}</span>;
      })}
    </span>
  );
}
```

**Key design decisions**:
- Uses `<mark>` element for semantic correctness and accessibility (screen readers announce highlighted text)
- Splits on word boundaries for multi-word queries ("login form" highlights "login" and "form" independently)
- Escapes regex special characters to avoid crashes on queries like "file.ts" or "auth()"
- Uses `bg-yellow-200/60` for light mode and `bg-yellow-800/40` for dark mode, which is subtle enough for a search highlight
- Returns plain `<span>` when no query, so it can be used unconditionally without conditional rendering

**Export from index**: Add to `/Users/evisdrenova/code/entire/devenv/entire.io/frontend/src/components/index.ts`:
```typescript
